WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.380
Hi, I'm Nei Maldaner,

2
00:00:01.380 --> 00:00:03.630
and this is track four of the

3
00:00:03.630 --> 00:00:04.620
LOOP-R course.

4
00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:06.360
The theme is measuring for real.

5
00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:08.180
This is the part that separates improvement

6
00:00:08.180 --> 00:00:09.420
from illusion.

7
00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:11.440
You'll learn how a target can be

8
00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:13.880
inflated without improving anything,

9
00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:16.060
how many executions a test needs before

10
00:00:16.060 --> 00:00:17.180
it starts,

11
00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:19.880
and how to write a yes-or-no checklist.

12
00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:21.880
Then you'll decide on a real card:

13
00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:23.640
approve, reject,

14
00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:26.900
or wait, with the rollback button within

15
00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:27.400
reach.

16
00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:28.380
Finally,

17
00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:30.300
an honest lesson about what the loop

18
00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:31.540
does not guarantee.

19
00:00:31.540 --> 00:00:33.560
We'll follow Renata's beauty clinic,

20
00:00:33.560 --> 00:00:35.180
Marcos the real estate agent,

21
00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:37.680
and Paula, the support manager.

22
00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:39.960
Every lesson has a short exercise.

23
00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:40.980
When I ask,

24
00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:42.680
pause and do it.

25
00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:45.120
There's an old rule in every business:

26
00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:47.040
when a measure becomes a target,

27
00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:48.100
it stops measuring.

28
00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:50.240
A learning system does the same thing,

29
00:00:50.240 --> 00:00:52.620
only faster and without feeling guilty.

30
00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:55.100
In LOOP-R, the target metric is the

31
00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:56.620
number you told the loop to raise.

32
00:00:56.620 --> 00:00:58.960
If that's the only number it watches,

33
00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:00.160
it

34
00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:01.580
finds the shortest path,

35
00:01:01.580 --> 00:01:04.300
and that path almost never means serving

36
00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:05.160
people better.

37
00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:06.980
The owner of the beauty clinic asked

38
00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:09.080
to increase the proposal response rate.

39
00:01:09.080 --> 00:01:10.260
Three cycles later,

40
00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:12.460
it went from twenty to thirty-four percent.

41
00:01:12.460 --> 00:01:13.460
The

42
00:01:13.460 --> 00:01:15.120
new version sent a second message the

43
00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:17.220
next day, and many replies said,

44
00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:19.620
“please stop sending me this.” The needle

45
00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:20.220
went up.

46
00:01:20.220 --> 00:01:21.500
The clinic didn't.

47
00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:22.360
The tricks repeat.

48
00:01:22.360 --> 00:01:24.840
Ask for more clicks and

49
00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:27.740
the loop learns clickbait headlines.

50
00:01:27.740 --> 00:01:30.420
Ask for shorter support times and it

51
00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:32.560
closes tickets without solving them.

52
00:01:32.560 --> 00:01:35.100
Ask for more sales and it discounts

53
00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:37.000
until the margin disappears.

54
00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:38.940
Ask for more replies and it learns

55
00:01:38.940 --> 00:01:40.140
to provoke people.

56
00:01:40.140 --> 00:01:42.240
The trick is in what got left

57
00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:42.840
out.

58
00:01:42.840 --> 00:01:45.360
The support manager wanted to bring average

59
00:01:45.360 --> 00:01:47.900
ticket time down from eighteen to ten

60
00:01:47.900 --> 00:01:48.460
minutes.

61
00:01:48.460 --> 00:01:50.160
In two weeks it reached nine.

62
00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:53.520
But tickets closed in two minutes reopened

63
00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:54.420
the next day,

64
00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:56.220
and satisfaction

65
00:01:56.220 --> 00:01:58.660
fell from four point three to three

66
00:01:58.660 --> 00:01:59.160
point six.

67
00:01:59.160 --> 00:02:01.220
The dashboard showed only time.

68
00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:03.360
When the target added “without

69
00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:06.840
worsening seven-day reopenings or satisfaction,” the same

70
00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:09.040
ticket started counting against the result.

71
00:02:09.040 --> 00:02:11.040
That's why, in LOOP-R,

72
00:02:11.040 --> 00:02:13.420
the target has a fixed form:

73
00:02:13.420 --> 00:02:16.040
maximize X without worsening Y,

74
00:02:16.040 --> 00:02:17.180
Z, and W.

75
00:02:17.180 --> 00:02:19.860
The numbers that must not fall are

76
00:02:19.860 --> 00:02:21.180
the guardrails.

77
00:02:21.180 --> 00:02:22.880
In sales, margin,

78
00:02:22.880 --> 00:02:24.660
complaints, unsubscribes,

79
00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:26.100
and average discount.

80
00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:28.300
In support, satisfaction

81
00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:30.460
and seven-day reopenings.

82
00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:32.400
Watch the numbers the most likely trick

83
00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:33.260
would affect.

84
00:02:33.260 --> 00:02:34.740
The real estate agent wrote:

85
00:02:34.740 --> 00:02:36.760
maximize visits booked per lead,

86
00:02:36.760 --> 00:02:37.780
without

87
00:02:37.780 --> 00:02:38.840
worsening

88
00:02:38.840 --> 00:02:41.500
no-show visits or the average discount.

89
00:02:41.500 --> 00:02:43.900
The Guardian vetoes a hypothesis that touches

90
00:02:43.900 --> 00:02:44.500
a guardrail.

91
00:02:44.500 --> 00:02:46.740
The Evaluator rejects a version that worsens

92
00:02:46.740 --> 00:02:49.600
a guardrail beyond its tolerance.

93
00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:52.340
Quick thought: replies rise by forty percent,

94
00:02:52.340 --> 00:02:54.180
margin falls by one percent,

95
00:02:54.180 --> 00:02:55.980
tolerance is zero.

96
00:02:55.980 --> 00:02:57.360
The Evaluator says:

97
00:02:57.360 --> 00:02:58.420
A stays.

98
00:02:58.420 --> 00:02:59.560
No exceptions.

99
00:02:59.560 --> 00:03:01.140
There's a quieter trick:

100
00:03:01.140 --> 00:03:03.160
the definition of the number.

101
00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:05.300
If a reply means any message back,

102
00:03:05.300 --> 00:03:08.000
“stop messaging me” counts as a reply.

103
00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:10.480
If resolved means any closed ticket,

104
00:03:10.480 --> 00:03:12.700
a ticket forcibly closed is resolved.

105
00:03:12.700 --> 00:03:14.880
That's why the

106
00:03:15.160 --> 00:03:16.960
definition goes on the loop worksheet,

107
00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:19.860
and the Observer checks the spreadsheet before

108
00:03:19.860 --> 00:03:21.220
adding things up.

109
00:03:21.220 --> 00:03:22.360
At the clinic,

110
00:03:22.360 --> 00:03:25.320
the spreadsheet gained a “positive reply” column.

111
00:03:25.320 --> 00:03:28.220
In support, it gained “reopened

112
00:03:28.220 --> 00:03:30.460
within seven days.” Now pause for about

113
00:03:30.460 --> 00:03:31.600
ten minutes.

114
00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:33.220
For Renata's, Marcos's,

115
00:03:33.220 --> 00:03:34.260
and Paula's targets,

116
00:03:34.260 --> 00:03:36.600
write the likeliest trick in one line

117
00:03:36.600 --> 00:03:38.240
and name two guardrails,

118
00:03:38.240 --> 00:03:40.000
then compare with the answer key.

119
00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:42.540
After that, rewrite the target for the

120
00:03:42.540 --> 00:03:44.820
process you chose in track two using

121
00:03:44.820 --> 00:03:46.060
this format.

122
00:03:46.060 --> 00:03:48.060
A target without a guardrail is not

123
00:03:48.060 --> 00:03:48.620
a target.

124
00:03:48.620 --> 00:03:49.780
It's an invitation.

125
00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:51.900
Flip a coin twelve times.

126
00:03:51.900 --> 00:03:53.820
Getting eight or more heads happens in

127
00:03:53.820 --> 00:03:55.440
almost one out of five tries,

128
00:03:55.440 --> 00:03:57.640
with no trick at all.

129
00:03:57.640 --> 00:04:00.000
Replace heads with a client who books.

130
00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:01.520
With twelve clients,

131
00:04:01.520 --> 00:04:03.400
a new message beating the old one

132
00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:05.320
is what chance would lead you to

133
00:04:05.320 --> 00:04:07.120
expect, not proof.

134
00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:09.420
The real estate agent changed the first

135
00:04:09.420 --> 00:04:11.520
message to portal leads.

136
00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:13.260
Of the next twelve leads,

137
00:04:13.260 --> 00:04:14.480
four booked a visit.

138
00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:16.140
With the old message,

139
00:04:16.140 --> 00:04:18.380
two of the previous twelve had booked.

140
00:04:18.380 --> 00:04:21.460
“It doubled,” he said in the meeting,

141
00:04:21.460 --> 00:04:24.260
and the new message went to everyone.

142
00:04:24.260 --> 00:04:26.280
Three weeks later the rate was where

143
00:04:26.280 --> 00:04:27.320
it had always been,

144
00:04:27.320 --> 00:04:29.620
and nobody knew whether the new message

145
00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:31.020
was better, worse,

146
00:04:31.020 --> 00:04:32.220
or

147
00:04:32.300 --> 00:04:32.900
the same.

148
00:04:32.900 --> 00:04:35.240
What he saw also happens when there

149
00:04:35.240 --> 00:04:36.580
is no difference at all.

150
00:04:36.580 --> 00:04:38.520
There's a standard calculation for this:

151
00:04:38.520 --> 00:04:39.940
the quantity that proves.

152
00:04:39.940 --> 00:04:41.840
The Experimenter does it and shows you

153
00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:43.000
before the test begins.

154
00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:44.680
You only need to read the table.

155
00:04:44.680 --> 00:04:47.207
From twenty to thirty percent takes about

156
00:04:47.207 --> 00:04:48.960
three hundred executions per version.

157
00:04:48.960 --> 00:04:50.740
From twenty to thirty-five,

158
00:04:50.740 --> 00:04:52.820
about one hundred forty.

159
00:04:52.820 --> 00:04:54.240
From three to five percent,

160
00:04:54.240 --> 00:04:55.440
about

161
00:04:55.484 --> 00:04:56.860
one thousand five hundred.

162
00:04:56.860 --> 00:04:58.600
The lower the starting point,

163
00:04:58.600 --> 00:05:00.060
the more executions.

164
00:05:00.060 --> 00:05:01.320
The bigger the increase,

165
00:05:01.320 --> 00:05:03.720
the fewer, as long as that increase

166
00:05:03.720 --> 00:05:06.000
is real and not just a wish.

167
00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:08.260
The clinic sends fifty proposals a week

168
00:05:08.260 --> 00:05:10.890
and wanted to raise sales conversion from

169
00:05:10.890 --> 00:05:12.169
three to five percent.

170
00:05:12.169 --> 00:05:14.420
One thousand five hundred with

171
00:05:14.420 --> 00:05:17.040
each version means sixty weeks for a

172
00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:18.440
single test.

173
00:05:18.640 --> 00:05:19.900
At that pace,

174
00:05:19.900 --> 00:05:21.440
you can't answer that question.

175
00:05:21.440 --> 00:05:23.180
The idea is to measure a number

176
00:05:23.180 --> 00:05:25.220
faster to get but still related to

177
00:05:25.220 --> 00:05:25.840
money.

178
00:05:25.840 --> 00:05:27.420
There are three kinds.

179
00:05:27.420 --> 00:05:29.200
Money: conversion,

180
00:05:30.160 --> 00:05:32.440
order value, margin;

181
00:05:32.440 --> 00:05:34.160
it takes months.

182
00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:36.220
Signal: reply, booking,

183
00:05:36.220 --> 00:05:39.000
useful click; it takes weeks.

184
00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:41.540
Artifact: does the text meet the checklist?

185
00:05:41.540 --> 00:05:43.120
You can see that in minutes.

186
00:05:43.120 --> 00:05:45.320
Run the test on the fastest number

187
00:05:45.320 --> 00:05:46.960
with a plausible link to money,

188
00:05:46.960 --> 00:05:49.120
and make money a guardrail.

189
00:05:49.120 --> 00:05:50.240
At the clinic,

190
00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:53.100
the target became replies from twenty to

191
00:05:53.100 --> 00:05:55.520
thirty percent, without worsening conversion.

192
00:05:55.520 --> 00:05:57.130
Three hundred per version,

193
00:05:57.130 --> 00:05:57.940
twelve weeks.

194
00:05:57.940 --> 00:06:00.480
In support, the money is contract renewal,

195
00:06:00.480 --> 00:06:02.480
the signal is resolved on first contact,

196
00:06:02.480 --> 00:06:04.420
and the artifact is whether the reply

197
00:06:04.420 --> 00:06:05.920
meets the checklist.

198
00:06:05.920 --> 00:06:07.760
The loop runs every week on the

199
00:06:07.760 --> 00:06:08.940
artifact and signal,

200
00:06:08.940 --> 00:06:10.420
and watches renewal.

201
00:06:10.420 --> 00:06:12.740
The Evaluator has only three answers:

202
00:06:12.740 --> 00:06:13.690
B

203
00:06:13.690 --> 00:06:15.040
won with margin,

204
00:06:15.040 --> 00:06:16.060
A

205
00:06:16.060 --> 00:06:18.120
stays, or insufficient sample.

206
00:06:18.120 --> 00:06:20.180
If the executions haven't reached the quantity

207
00:06:20.180 --> 00:06:22.340
that proves, the answer is the third

208
00:06:22.340 --> 00:06:22.840
one.

209
00:06:22.720 --> 00:06:23.720
Always.

210
00:06:23.720 --> 00:06:25.720
Stopping early because you're winning is the

211
00:06:25.720 --> 00:06:27.300
most common way to turn noise into

212
00:06:27.300 --> 00:06:28.360
a rule.

213
00:06:28.360 --> 00:06:30.440
The only early stop is when a

214
00:06:30.440 --> 00:06:30.940
guardrail falls.

215
00:06:30.940 --> 00:06:32.160
At the clinic,

216
00:06:32.160 --> 00:06:34.120
the first cycle almost started the wrong

217
00:06:34.120 --> 00:06:36.580
way: with the small effect the Optimizer

218
00:06:36.580 --> 00:06:38.880
expected, the test would take forty weeks.

219
00:06:38.880 --> 00:06:40.720
The owner resized it around the worksheet

220
00:06:40.720 --> 00:06:43.220
target: three hundred per version.

221
00:06:43.220 --> 00:06:45.880
Week five for the real estate agent:

222
00:06:45.880 --> 00:06:48.760
message B has a thirty-one percent booking

223
00:06:48.760 --> 00:06:50.000
rate versus

224
00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:52.520
twenty-two, with one hundred forty leads on

225
00:06:52.520 --> 00:06:53.320
each side.

226
00:06:53.320 --> 00:06:55.780
The target is three hundred.

227
00:06:55.780 --> 00:06:57.840
The answer: continue.

228
00:06:58.000 --> 00:06:59.220
Insufficient sample.

229
00:06:59.220 --> 00:07:00.860
Once the loop counts things,

230
00:07:00.860 --> 00:07:02.460
the Critic will want to split them

231
00:07:02.460 --> 00:07:03.520
by client type,

232
00:07:03.520 --> 00:07:05.680
channel, or day of the week.

233
00:07:05.680 --> 00:07:07.740
Every slice follows the same rule.

234
00:07:07.740 --> 00:07:09.940
Call it a pattern only with thirty

235
00:07:09.940 --> 00:07:11.820
executions in that slice.

236
00:07:11.820 --> 00:07:14.520
Ninety or more is strong and becomes

237
00:07:14.520 --> 00:07:15.960
a priority hypothesis.

238
00:07:15.960 --> 00:07:18.660
From thirty to eighty-nine is moderate and

239
00:07:18.660 --> 00:07:19.840
becomes a hypothesis.

240
00:07:19.840 --> 00:07:22.300
Below thirty is weak and goes into

241
00:07:22.300 --> 00:07:23.360
memory as observed,

242
00:07:23.360 --> 00:07:24.220
not tested.

243
00:07:24.220 --> 00:07:25.300
At the clinic,

244
00:07:25.300 --> 00:07:27.900
facial treatments seemed to get more replies

245
00:07:27.900 --> 00:07:29.440
than body treatments,

246
00:07:29.440 --> 00:07:31.700
fourteen versus eleven.

247
00:07:31.700 --> 00:07:32.980
That was saved,

248
00:07:32.980 --> 00:07:34.160
and three months later,

249
00:07:34.160 --> 00:07:35.520
with sixty of each,

250
00:07:35.520 --> 00:07:37.800
it became a moderate hypothesis.

251
00:07:37.800 --> 00:07:39.560
Now pause for about ten minutes.

252
00:07:39.560 --> 00:07:40.500
For the clinic,

253
00:07:40.500 --> 00:07:42.420
real estate, and support,

254
00:07:42.420 --> 00:07:44.100
choose a

255
00:07:44.520 --> 00:07:46.320
realistic metric,

256
00:07:46.400 --> 00:07:47.880
executions per version,

257
00:07:47.880 --> 00:07:49.640
and number of weeks.

258
00:07:49.640 --> 00:07:51.280
Read per version,

259
00:07:51.280 --> 00:07:52.960
not as a total.

260
00:07:53.160 --> 00:07:54.980
When the result depends on the client,

261
00:07:54.980 --> 00:07:56.780
the test takes weeks.

262
00:07:56.780 --> 00:07:58.180
But much of what you want to

263
00:07:58.180 --> 00:08:00.740
know is right there in the text.

264
00:08:00.740 --> 00:08:02.470
The problem is that a score from

265
00:08:02.470 --> 00:08:03.800
one to ten doesn't work.

266
00:08:03.800 --> 00:08:05.380
Two people give it a seven and

267
00:08:05.380 --> 00:08:07.160
an eight, and both are right,

268
00:08:07.160 --> 00:08:08.740
because you can't check what a seven

269
00:08:08.740 --> 00:08:09.860
means.

270
00:08:09.860 --> 00:08:12.060
Text judges prefer the longer version,

271
00:08:12.060 --> 00:08:13.460
the second one they read,

272
00:08:13.460 --> 00:08:15.000
and they change their minds.

273
00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:16.720
The answer isn't to find a better

274
00:08:16.720 --> 00:08:17.260
judge.

275
00:08:17.260 --> 00:08:18.740
It's to change the question.

276
00:08:18.740 --> 00:08:21.840
“Is this proposal good?” can't be checked.

277
00:08:21.840 --> 00:08:24.860
“Does it have exactly one closing question?”

278
00:08:24.860 --> 00:08:26.480
is yes or no.

279
00:08:26.480 --> 00:08:28.540
The clinic owner replaced

280
00:08:28.540 --> 00:08:31.000
“make it better” with questions like:

281
00:08:31.000 --> 00:08:33.740
does it mention something the client said,

282
00:08:33.740 --> 00:08:35.640
is it at most eighty words,

283
00:08:35.640 --> 00:08:37.240
does it promise a timeline?

284
00:08:37.240 --> 00:08:38.360
For the first time,

285
00:08:38.360 --> 00:08:40.720
she and the receptionist started giving the

286
00:08:40.720 --> 00:08:41.700
same answers.

287
00:08:41.700 --> 00:08:43.620
The model checklist looks like a car

288
00:08:43.620 --> 00:08:44.870
inspection form.

289
00:08:44.870 --> 00:08:46.760
Seven questions for a proposal.

290
00:08:46.760 --> 00:08:48.560
Is it at most eighty words?

291
00:08:48.560 --> 00:08:51.240
Does the first sentence mention something the

292
00:08:51.240 --> 00:08:51.860
client said?

293
00:08:51.860 --> 00:08:54.040
Is there exactly one closing question?

294
00:08:54.040 --> 00:08:56.320
Does it avoid promising a timeline?

295
00:08:56.320 --> 00:08:58.360
Is the discount at most ten percent?

296
00:08:58.360 --> 00:09:00.460
No mistakes about the product?

297
00:09:00.460 --> 00:09:02.780
A tone with no double exclamation marks,

298
00:09:02.780 --> 00:09:04.960
“don't miss out,” or all caps?

299
00:09:04.960 --> 00:09:06.360
Two are invariants,

300
00:09:06.360 --> 00:09:08.480
taken from answer three on the worksheet,

301
00:09:08.480 --> 00:09:10.180
and failing either one in a single

302
00:09:10.180 --> 00:09:11.840
case sinks the version.

303
00:09:11.840 --> 00:09:13.080
To write yours,

304
00:09:13.080 --> 00:09:15.440
set aside five approved texts and five

305
00:09:15.440 --> 00:09:17.100
sent back.

306
00:09:17.100 --> 00:09:19.260
Turn what the good ones have into

307
00:09:19.260 --> 00:09:19.860
questions.

308
00:09:19.860 --> 00:09:22.640
Cut any question that needs an “it

309
00:09:22.640 --> 00:09:23.840
depends.”

310
00:09:24.240 --> 00:09:26.860
Ask someone else to answer without talking

311
00:09:26.860 --> 00:09:29.280
to you, and rewrite the questions where

312
00:09:29.280 --> 00:09:30.020
you disagree.

313
00:09:30.020 --> 00:09:30.900
Day to day,

314
00:09:30.900 --> 00:09:33.120
the Evaluator answers the checklist,

315
00:09:33.120 --> 00:09:34.860
and it needs to be checked against

316
00:09:34.860 --> 00:09:36.920
you because judges drift.

317
00:09:36.920 --> 00:09:39.140
This is the loop's only manual measurement

318
00:09:39.140 --> 00:09:40.200
task:

319
00:09:40.200 --> 00:09:43.220
you answer yes or no for ten

320
00:09:43.220 --> 00:09:44.590
to twenty texts.

321
00:09:44.590 --> 00:09:46.220
Twenty minutes, once.

322
00:09:46.220 --> 00:09:49.280
Each cycle, the Evaluator answers the same

323
00:09:49.280 --> 00:09:49.880
texts.

324
00:09:49.880 --> 00:09:51.780
If it agrees with you less than

325
00:09:51.780 --> 00:09:52.820
eighty percent of the time,

326
00:09:52.820 --> 00:09:54.580
the judge is uncalibrated,

327
00:09:54.580 --> 00:09:55.960
nothing is promoted,

328
00:09:55.960 --> 00:09:57.880
and the Meta-agent alerts you.

329
00:09:57.880 --> 00:10:00.340
If a question scores below eighty percent,

330
00:10:00.340 --> 00:10:02.920
rewrite or remove it.

331
00:10:02.920 --> 00:10:05.960
The support manager calibrated it with fifteen

332
00:10:05.960 --> 00:10:06.980
replies:

333
00:10:06.980 --> 00:10:08.180
seventy-one percent.

334
00:10:08.180 --> 00:10:09.140
The

335
00:10:09.140 --> 00:10:10.840
culprit was the question,

336
00:10:10.840 --> 00:10:13.240
“Is the reply courteous?” She changed it,

337
00:10:13.240 --> 00:10:15.260
and the score reached

338
00:10:15.260 --> 00:10:16.380
ninety-three percent.

339
00:10:16.380 --> 00:10:18.560
A text's score is the number of

340
00:10:18.560 --> 00:10:19.600
yes answers.

341
00:10:19.600 --> 00:10:21.000
To compare versions,

342
00:10:21.000 --> 00:10:22.740
the loop uses twenty to fifty saved

343
00:10:22.740 --> 00:10:25.080
cases, called checklist cases.

344
00:10:25.080 --> 00:10:27.220
B wins if its average is at

345
00:10:27.220 --> 00:10:29.560
least one criterion higher and it doesn't

346
00:10:29.560 --> 00:10:31.860
lose on any invariant in any case.

347
00:10:31.860 --> 00:10:34.300
The real estate agent saved

348
00:10:34.300 --> 00:10:35.260
thirty old leads.

349
00:10:35.260 --> 00:10:37.840
The new version averaged five point four

350
00:10:37.840 --> 00:10:38.760
against

351
00:10:38.760 --> 00:10:40.200
four point one,

352
00:10:40.200 --> 00:10:42.160
but in one of the thirty cases

353
00:10:42.160 --> 00:10:44.160
it quoted a price below the listed

354
00:10:44.160 --> 00:10:44.740
amount.

355
00:10:44.740 --> 00:10:45.880
It lost.

356
00:10:45.880 --> 00:10:48.080
Now pause for about fifteen minutes.

357
00:10:48.080 --> 00:10:50.120
Take the text your AI produces most

358
00:10:50.120 --> 00:10:51.060
often,

359
00:10:51.060 --> 00:10:53.560
set aside three approved examples and three

360
00:10:53.560 --> 00:10:55.360
returned ones, and

361
00:10:55.360 --> 00:10:56.840
write six

362
00:10:56.840 --> 00:11:00.080
yes-or-no questions, including two invariants.

363
00:11:00.080 --> 00:11:02.060
Ask another person to answer for the

364
00:11:02.060 --> 00:11:02.560
same texts.

365
00:11:02.560 --> 00:11:04.760
You're done when they can fill in

366
00:11:04.760 --> 00:11:06.980
all thirty-six boxes without asking,

367
00:11:06.980 --> 00:11:08.180
“what

368
00:11:08.320 --> 00:11:09.493
does it depend on?”

369
00:11:09.520 --> 00:11:10.520
After the test,

370
00:11:10.520 --> 00:11:11.400
someone has to say:

371
00:11:11.400 --> 00:11:13.620
make this the official version.

372
00:11:13.620 --> 00:11:15.420
That's what the decision card is for,

373
00:11:15.420 --> 00:11:16.800
and it's the only thing the loop

374
00:11:16.800 --> 00:11:18.240
asks you to pay attention to.

375
00:11:18.240 --> 00:11:21.440
It arrives at most once a week,

376
00:11:21.440 --> 00:11:23.260
with five lines:

377
00:11:23.260 --> 00:11:25.600
hypothesis, result with quantity and margin,

378
00:11:25.600 --> 00:11:26.540
guardrails,

379
00:11:26.540 --> 00:11:27.880
cost against the ceiling,

380
00:11:27.880 --> 00:11:28.720
and decision.

381
00:11:28.720 --> 00:11:30.540
Read from top to bottom.

382
00:11:30.540 --> 00:11:32.980
Approve: the candidate becomes official.

383
00:11:32.980 --> 00:11:35.860
Reject: the current version stays,

384
00:11:35.860 --> 00:11:39.020
and the hypothesis goes into memory with

385
00:11:39.020 --> 00:11:39.760
the reason.

386
00:11:39.760 --> 00:11:42.440
Wait: the test continues.

387
00:11:42.520 --> 00:11:43.500
With no answer,

388
00:11:43.500 --> 00:11:46.300
nothing is promoted and the decision stays

389
00:11:46.300 --> 00:11:46.960
pending.

390
00:11:46.960 --> 00:11:49.280
The real estate agent left a card

391
00:11:49.280 --> 00:11:50.500
unopened for three days,

392
00:11:50.500 --> 00:11:52.600
and the old version kept replying.

393
00:11:52.600 --> 00:11:55.340
The common mistake is approving because the

394
00:11:55.340 --> 00:11:56.560
new one looks better.

395
00:11:56.560 --> 00:11:58.660
Approve only when line two says B

396
00:11:58.660 --> 00:11:59.760
won with margin,

397
00:11:59.760 --> 00:12:01.360
with the minimum quantity.

398
00:12:01.360 --> 00:12:02.900
In the clinic's second cycle,

399
00:12:02.900 --> 00:12:05.060
the hypothesis was a proposal of at

400
00:12:05.060 --> 00:12:07.020
most eighty words.

401
00:12:07.020 --> 00:12:09.303
Replies went from nineteen point three to

402
00:12:09.303 --> 00:12:10.434
twenty-nine point seven percent,

403
00:12:10.434 --> 00:12:12.170
three hundred on each side.

404
00:12:12.170 --> 00:12:14.000
Ten points, and not by luck.

405
00:12:14.000 --> 00:12:15.660
But complaints were six versus one,

406
00:12:15.660 --> 00:12:17.540
with zero tolerance.

407
00:12:17.860 --> 00:12:20.120
Verdict: A stays.

408
00:12:20.280 --> 00:12:22.500
The mistake was in the rule.

409
00:12:22.500 --> 00:12:24.340
A complaint is a rare event,

410
00:12:24.340 --> 00:12:25.220
about one percent,

411
00:12:25.220 --> 00:12:27.140
and six versus one out of three

412
00:12:27.140 --> 00:12:28.880
hundred can easily happen by chance.

413
00:12:28.880 --> 00:12:29.960
It

414
00:12:29.960 --> 00:12:30.620
was noise.

415
00:12:30.620 --> 00:12:32.980
The lesson isn't to ignore a guardrail

416
00:12:32.980 --> 00:12:34.940
when the gain is large.

417
00:12:34.940 --> 00:12:36.760
It's to calculate tolerance:

418
00:12:36.760 --> 00:12:38.960
here, zero point zero one,

419
00:12:38.960 --> 00:12:39.990
not

420
00:12:39.990 --> 00:12:40.490
zero.

421
00:12:40.420 --> 00:12:42.220
The owner adjusted the worksheet,

422
00:12:42.220 --> 00:12:45.480
and two cycles later another hypothesis truly

423
00:12:45.480 --> 00:12:45.980
won.

424
00:12:45.900 --> 00:12:48.060
The cost line is there because you

425
00:12:48.060 --> 00:12:49.980
wrote a ceiling on the worksheet.

426
00:12:49.980 --> 00:12:51.320
It's answer four:

427
00:12:51.320 --> 00:12:53.240
how much a cycle can cost in

428
00:12:53.240 --> 00:12:54.960
money and how much of your time

429
00:12:54.960 --> 00:12:56.500
it needs each week.

430
00:12:56.500 --> 00:12:58.880
The Guardian stops the cycle at the

431
00:12:58.880 --> 00:12:59.380
ceiling.

432
00:12:59.140 --> 00:13:01.680
And the Meta-agent watches the cost per

433
00:13:01.680 --> 00:13:03.200
promoted hypothesis:

434
00:13:03.620 --> 00:13:05.680
if nothing has been promoted in five

435
00:13:05.680 --> 00:13:06.660
cycles,

436
00:13:06.660 --> 00:13:08.220
it suggests running

437
00:13:08.220 --> 00:13:10.440
less often, using cheaper assistants,

438
00:13:10.440 --> 00:13:12.340
or loading less memory.

439
00:13:12.340 --> 00:13:14.520
The support manager set sixty reais per

440
00:13:14.520 --> 00:13:16.440
cycle and one hour of her time

441
00:13:16.440 --> 00:13:16.940
a week.

442
00:13:16.760 --> 00:13:17.960
Answer

443
00:13:18.140 --> 00:13:20.420
five is who approves.

444
00:13:20.420 --> 00:13:21.380
At L zero,

445
00:13:21.380 --> 00:13:23.360
the loop only reports.

446
00:13:23.360 --> 00:13:24.260
At L one,

447
00:13:24.260 --> 00:13:26.080
you approve every card.

448
00:13:26.080 --> 00:13:26.700
At L two,

449
00:13:26.700 --> 00:13:29.480
it promotes on its own and

450
00:13:29.480 --> 00:13:31.780
alerts you, but only after five correct

451
00:13:31.780 --> 00:13:33.360
promotions at L one.

452
00:13:33.360 --> 00:13:35.800
Always start at L one.

453
00:13:35.800 --> 00:13:38.340
The next lesson explains why L three

454
00:13:38.340 --> 00:13:39.540
is still research.

455
00:13:39.540 --> 00:13:41.940
What makes L two acceptable is the

456
00:13:41.940 --> 00:13:42.700
rollback button.

457
00:13:42.700 --> 00:13:44.700
In the cycle after a promotion,

458
00:13:44.700 --> 00:13:46.660
if the test number or a guardrail

459
00:13:46.660 --> 00:13:49.640
falls below what the previous version achieved,

460
00:13:49.640 --> 00:13:53.100
beyond tolerance, the previous version returns.

461
00:13:53.760 --> 00:13:54.800
At L one,

462
00:13:54.800 --> 00:13:56.480
the card asks you to confirm.

463
00:13:56.480 --> 00:13:57.540
At L two,

464
00:13:57.540 --> 00:13:59.400
it rolls back on its own and

465
00:13:59.400 --> 00:14:00.200
alerts you.

466
00:14:00.200 --> 00:14:02.460
The real estate agent promoted a reply

467
00:14:02.460 --> 00:14:03.440
in cycle five.

468
00:14:03.440 --> 00:14:04.760
In cycle six,

469
00:14:04.760 --> 00:14:07.180
bookings fell from thirty-one to nineteen percent,

470
00:14:07.180 --> 00:14:09.340
below the old version's twenty-two.

471
00:14:09.340 --> 00:14:10.320
He rolled it back,

472
00:14:10.320 --> 00:14:12.040
and the version stayed in the history

473
00:14:12.040 --> 00:14:13.380
as reverted.

474
00:14:13.380 --> 00:14:15.500
Now pause for about twelve minutes.

475
00:14:15.500 --> 00:14:17.280
Decide on the three practice cards,

476
00:14:17.280 --> 00:14:19.060
with your reason in one line.

477
00:14:19.060 --> 00:14:21.260
Then write answers four and five on

478
00:14:21.260 --> 00:14:22.680
your worksheet as numbers:

479
00:14:22.680 --> 00:14:24.900
ceiling, time, starting

480
00:14:24.900 --> 00:14:26.780
level, deadline for the card,

481
00:14:26.780 --> 00:14:28.520
and condition for moving up.

482
00:14:28.520 --> 00:14:30.700
No learning loop guarantees that a number

483
00:14:30.700 --> 00:14:32.030
will rise.

484
00:14:32.030 --> 00:14:32.940
LOOP-R

485
00:14:32.940 --> 00:14:33.880
guarantees

486
00:14:33.880 --> 00:14:36.020
four things by design.

487
00:14:36.020 --> 00:14:38.660
A worse version never replaces the current

488
00:14:38.660 --> 00:14:40.600
one by a system decision.

489
00:14:40.600 --> 00:14:43.080
Every change has a record and a

490
00:14:43.080 --> 00:14:43.800
rollback.

491
00:14:43.800 --> 00:14:46.260
The cycle always runs the same way.

492
00:14:46.260 --> 00:14:48.280
Cost does not exceed the ceiling.

493
00:14:48.280 --> 00:14:51.200
Each guarantee has a matching limit.

494
00:14:51.200 --> 00:14:53.740
Keeping a worse version out doesn't mean

495
00:14:53.740 --> 00:14:55.520
the next one will be better.

496
00:14:55.520 --> 00:14:57.180
Having a record doesn't mean it will

497
00:14:57.180 --> 00:14:58.520
contain anything useful.

498
00:14:58.520 --> 00:15:01.440
Running every time doesn't mean every cycle

499
00:15:01.440 --> 00:15:02.960
brings a good hypothesis.

500
00:15:02.960 --> 00:15:05.160
Staying under the ceiling doesn't mean the

501
00:15:05.160 --> 00:15:06.860
cost is worthwhile.

502
00:15:07.020 --> 00:15:08.880
If you read “guaranteed to bring more

503
00:15:08.880 --> 00:15:11.380
sales” about any AI loop,

504
00:15:11.380 --> 00:15:12.480
including this one,

505
00:15:12.480 --> 00:15:14.700
that's a promise nobody can make.

506
00:15:14.700 --> 00:15:15.540
In lesson two,

507
00:15:15.540 --> 00:15:18.240
you replaced money with a signal as

508
00:15:18.240 --> 00:15:18.820
the target.

509
00:15:18.820 --> 00:15:20.380
That comes at a price:

510
00:15:20.380 --> 00:15:22.620
raising the signal does not prove that

511
00:15:22.620 --> 00:15:24.180
money will rise.

512
00:15:24.180 --> 00:15:27.140
It's plausible, but plausible doesn't mean proven.

513
00:15:27.140 --> 00:15:28.820
In the clinic's fourth cycle,

514
00:15:28.820 --> 00:15:31.256
replies went from nineteen point three to

515
00:15:31.256 --> 00:15:32.360
twenty-nine point three percent,

516
00:15:32.360 --> 00:15:34.660
and the version was rightly promoted.

517
00:15:34.660 --> 00:15:36.872
Conversion went from three to three point

518
00:15:36.872 --> 00:15:38.280
seven percent, which,

519
00:15:38.280 --> 00:15:39.900
with three hundred on each side,

520
00:15:39.900 --> 00:15:41.880
cannot be distinguished from chance.

521
00:15:41.880 --> 00:15:43.180
The report says:

522
00:15:43.180 --> 00:15:45.480
the link between signal and target remains

523
00:15:45.480 --> 00:15:46.250
unproven.

524
00:15:46.250 --> 00:15:48.340
Replies truly went up;

525
00:15:48.340 --> 00:15:50.620
there is still no proof about sales,

526
00:15:50.620 --> 00:15:53.240
and the version can be promoted anyway.

527
00:15:53.240 --> 00:15:55.740
The real estate agent faces the same

528
00:15:55.740 --> 00:15:58.420
thing: more visits have not yet proven

529
00:15:58.420 --> 00:15:59.460
more sales.

530
00:15:59.460 --> 00:16:02.160
The loop guarantees that the cycle runs

531
00:16:02.160 --> 00:16:04.280
every week, not that the week brings

532
00:16:04.280 --> 00:16:05.840
a good idea.

533
00:16:05.840 --> 00:16:07.080
In a small business,

534
00:16:07.080 --> 00:16:08.880
it's common for history to pile up

535
00:16:08.880 --> 00:16:10.220
without enough evidence,

536
00:16:10.220 --> 00:16:11.500
cycle after cycle.

537
00:16:11.500 --> 00:16:13.640
That doesn't mean the loop is broken.

538
00:16:13.640 --> 00:16:15.520
It means the

539
00:16:15.680 --> 00:16:17.560
loop is telling the truth about the

540
00:16:17.560 --> 00:16:18.420
volume it has.

541
00:16:18.420 --> 00:16:21.320
The support manager had six cycles like

542
00:16:21.320 --> 00:16:23.240
that, reduced the loop to every other

543
00:16:23.240 --> 00:16:25.440
week, as the Meta-agent suggested,

544
00:16:25.440 --> 00:16:28.640
and in June the first moderate hypothesis

545
00:16:28.640 --> 00:16:29.420
arrived.

546
00:16:29.420 --> 00:16:31.400
A loop that redesigns itself,

547
00:16:31.400 --> 00:16:32.420
level L three,

548
00:16:32.420 --> 00:16:33.780
is still research:

549
00:16:33.780 --> 00:16:34.880
in the product,

550
00:16:34.880 --> 00:16:37.220
the Meta-agent only reports.

551
00:16:37.340 --> 00:16:39.740
And the bottleneck no assistant can solve

552
00:16:39.740 --> 00:16:41.580
is the log spreadsheet.

553
00:16:41.580 --> 00:16:43.220
Now pause for about eight minutes.

554
00:16:43.220 --> 00:16:44.120
Mark

555
00:16:44.120 --> 00:16:46.760
true or false for the eight statements

556
00:16:46.760 --> 00:16:47.880
in

557
00:16:47.880 --> 00:16:50.240
the exercise, and for each false one,

558
00:16:50.240 --> 00:16:53.080
write which real guarantee it stretches.

559
00:16:53.080 --> 00:16:55.300
A target never stands alone:

560
00:16:55.300 --> 00:16:57.580
maximize X without worsening Y and Z,

561
00:16:57.580 --> 00:16:59.740
with the number clearly defined.

562
00:16:59.740 --> 00:17:02.320
Before testing, you know how many executions

563
00:17:02.320 --> 00:17:03.520
prove

564
00:17:03.580 --> 00:17:05.660
the result and how many weeks it

565
00:17:05.660 --> 00:17:08.080
takes, and you test the fastest signal

566
00:17:08.080 --> 00:17:09.560
while watching the money.

567
00:17:09.560 --> 00:17:10.520
Before

568
00:17:10.520 --> 00:17:11.560
the finish line,

569
00:17:11.560 --> 00:17:14.380
there is only an insufficient sample.

570
00:17:14.380 --> 00:17:16.260
For text, you

571
00:17:16.260 --> 00:17:18.760
have a yes-or-no checklist checked with another

572
00:17:18.760 --> 00:17:19.440
person.

573
00:17:19.440 --> 00:17:21.040
When it's time to decide,

574
00:17:21.040 --> 00:17:22.780
you read the five-line card from top

575
00:17:22.780 --> 00:17:25.020
to bottom, start at L one,

576
00:17:25.020 --> 00:17:27.080
and always have the rollback button.

577
00:17:27.080 --> 00:17:29.320
And you know what the loop guarantees,

578
00:17:29.320 --> 00:17:31.680
and what nobody can guarantee.

579
00:17:31.820 --> 00:17:33.000
In track five,

580
00:17:33.000 --> 00:17:35.120
you'll follow the clinic's four real cycles

581
00:17:35.120 --> 00:17:37.300
from beginning to end,

582
00:17:37.300 --> 00:17:38.280
